cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DXA Data Extractor"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hoch
    given-names: "Jonathan W."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4992-1199"
    affiliation: "Cardiovascular and Applied Physiology Laboratory, Florida State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/dxa-extractor"
url: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/dxa-extractor"
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
abstract: >-
  Command-line tool for batch-extracting body composition and bone density
  results from Hologic DXA PDF reports into a single CSV file, built for
  longitudinal research studies with pre/post or multi-timepoint scan designs.
  Identifies report pages by content, reads regional fat, lean and bone
  mineral content, bone mineral density with T- and Z-scores, android and
  gynoid regions, visceral adipose tissue and the adipose and lean indices,
  keeps the most precise printed copy of each value, flags limbs the scanner
  mirrored from the opposite side, and checks each report's internal
  arithmetic.
keywords:
  - dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry
  - DXA
  - body composition
  - bone mineral density
  - visceral adipose tissue
  - PDF data extraction
  - research data management
